{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386020-unerring-judgement-orichalcum-dragon-sigh-wand-\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7-wip","id":1386020,"title":"Unerring Judgement (Orichalcum Dragon Sigh Wand \u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7) WIP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-06T00:19:50-07:00","id":1386020,"title":"Unerring Judgement (Orichalcum Dragon Sigh Wand \u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7) WIP","content":"This artifact is a bit of an experiment based around a few ideas. Firstly, I wanted to try out making an artifact where I don't rush to get rid of the Slow tag but actually make the time investment worthwhile and reward planning a few turns ahead. I also have wanted to make a sniper-like long range firewand for a while, so this seemed like the perfect time. I've got the bread-and-butter effects down, but I'm struggling to come up with high level effects that don't feel redundant with existing Archery or RDS charms, so I'd appreciate some ideas. All feedback is welcome!<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Unerring Judgement (Orichalcum Dragon Sigh Wand \u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7)</b></span><br /> <br /> Artifact Heavy Archery Weapon<br /> Accuracy: close: - short: +5 medium: +3 long: +1<br /> Damage: +14 Overwhelming 5<br /> Tags: Lethal, Archery (Long), Flame, Slow<br /> <br /> Unerring Judgement is a marvel of First Age engineering that defies the common practices and limitations of traditional firedust weaponry. Its long and slender barrel, though unwieldy, allows it to project concentrated bursts of flame with remarkable accuracy over long distances. It was commissioned from the forge-cathedrals of Dehelesen by the Night Caste Seven-Eyed Dreamer, who wielded it to hunt down and eradicate the Fair Folk all across the Burning Sands and the wylds beyond, reality engines following in his wake in the first great expansion of Creation's borders. It was taken as a prize during the Balorian Crusade, then recovered by a hearth of Dragon-Blooded who slew the raksha prince who had claimed it. In the Age of Sorrows, it was last recorded to be in the possession of a guild factor who is convinced he'll make a fortune as soon as he can figure out how to replicate its barrel to use on mundane firewands.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement Bonus: </b>Unerring Judgement\u2019s elongated barrel is optimized for long range shooting, launching bursts of fire that grows in speed and power the further they travel. It adds +1 automatic success to all attack and damage rolls made at medium range, +2 at long range and +3 at extreme range or further. However, this comes at a significant cost: the weapon is unwieldy and requires bracing; it cannot be fired at all if there\u2019s an active hostile character within close range of the shooter.<br /> Additionally, the weapon is incompatible with charms that create multiple attacks, such as Trance of Unhesitating Speed and Revolving Bow Discipline. Charms which fire multiple projectiles but involve only a single attack roll, such as Arrow Storm Technique or Arrow Rain Tempest, can still be used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Evocations of Unerring Judgement:</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Bottled Lightning Concentration:</b><br /> Cost: varies; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Until Fired<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> The shooter opens the breech and loads a new charge of firedust, infusing it with her essence and killing intent.<br /> This Evocation supplements an action to load the weapon that cannot be quickened in any way. She may choose any number of compatible attack-enhancing Supplemental or Simple charms and pay their cost now. Their effects will apply to the next shot she takes.<br /> Each charm used in this way has their cost reduced by 1 mote, and the total cost of all charms is reduced by 1 willpower. If this expenditure of essence would cause her anima to increase, it is delayed until the moment when she fires. An unfired charge loses its potency at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Breathing and Killing Meditation:</b><br /> Cost: -; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> Unerring Judgement\u2019s heavy frame offers unparalleled stability, and its blue jade magnifying crystals reward the patient shooter with accuracy befitting of its name.<br /> This Evocation permanently improves aim actions with this weapon, granting Perception bonus dice to the attack roll instead of the usual 3, and the shooter only needs to aim once to gain the accuracy bonus even at medium range or beyond.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Searing Light of Judgement:</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Breathing and Killing Meditation<br /> The flames of Unerring Judgement flash like shooting stars and explode like meteors, disorienting its enemies.<br /> A target hit by this attack is blinded until the end of the shooter\u2019s next turn. If the damage roll successes exceed their Wits, they are disoriented and treat all ground as difficult terrain for the same duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Deadly Hunter\u2019s Preparations:</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Until Fired<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Bottled Lighting Concentration<br /> With growing familiarity, the shooter learns to customize the mix of firedust in her shots to better adapt to a variety of opponents.<br /> When loading the weapon with the prerequisite, she may choose to add one of the following custom mixes. Upon learning this Evocation, she learns two of these mixes; additional ones can be learned for 3xp each.<br /> <br /> <b>Kingslayer\u2019s Recipe: </b>when hunting high-profile targets, bodyguards are a common complication. A fast-burning reagent makes the shot faster and more difficult to intercept.<br /> When fired at a target benefitting from a Defend Other action, if her attack roll beats the defender\u2019s Defence, they take Essence dice of lethal damage ignoring Hardness and the shot continues unimpeded \u2013 she may apply her full attack successes against the original target\u2019s Defence and her damage is not reduced.<br /> <br /> <b>Titan\u2019s Sneeze: </b>walls and shields can usually complicate a shot, but this high-temperature fuel takes care of the sturdiest of barriers.<br /> This shot ignores and destroys any cover not made of the five magical materials, and mundane weapons used to parry it are destroyed.<br /> <br /> <b>Big Game Buster:</b> large beasts can be a large problem, that\u2019s why the experienced hunter always comes loaded for yeddim.<br /> When fired at a target of Legendary Size, ignore the limit on decisive damage. If used against a Warstrider, the shooter may forgo 9 levels of damage to make an automatically successful Breach Frame gambit and apply the rest of the damage against the pilot directly.<br /> <br /> <b>Scattershot Special: </b>sometimes to get to a mark you have to get through a horde of minions or two. A mix of firedust and shrapnel takes care of crowds handily.<br /> When fired at a battlegroup, the attack inflicts an automatic level of damage for every 2 damage dice instead of every 4. If this results in a rout check, increase the difficulty by 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Stampede-Stalling Fusillade:</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Resonant<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Deadly Hunter\u2019s Preparations<br /> The weapon\u2019s blasts carry such force that even when they fail to kill the target outright, they whittle their momentum and leave them vulnerable.<br /> After damage is resolved, the target loses initiative equal to the number of range bands between them and the shooter +1. If this initiative loss crashes them, they lose their next movement action.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonant: </b>the shooter adds an equal amount of initiative to her base after resetting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":10131,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","user":"BadassOverlord","date":". 05-06-2020, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}